# Case A — **Purely visual color change** (no physical/material change)

| Phase                             | Module                                                 | Impact                                                                                                                                                                 |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 2. 3D Modeling                    | **CAD CRUD**                                           | New part/assembly *revision* to store the appearance tweak. Keep `partUUID` the same.                                                                                  |
| 6. Documentation & Change Control | **DocGen**                                             | Update renders/drawings/screenshots; ECO can be **minor/appearance-only**. Pack manifests unchanged.                                                                   |
| 8. Inspection & Testing           | **VisionQC**                                           | Small: if your CV models compare photos vs. expected appearance, retrain/whitelist the new color to avoid false “defect” flags. Geometry/face mapping unaffected.      |
| 7. Production & Assembly          | **MES Sync**                                           | Usually **no change** (work orders are same). If your travelers include color callouts (paint code), ensure the appearance note doesn’t propagate as a process change. |
| 9. Deployment & In-Service        | **FieldLink**                                          | None, unless field UIs render color-coded parts—then update the viewer assets.                                                                                         |
| 1,3,4,5,10                        | **RQ Linker, MatCalc, ProxyFEA, PathGen, Prognostics** | **No impact**—physics, mass, cost, and processes are unchanged.                                                                                                        |

# Case B — **Material change** (e.g., 6061-T6 → 7075-T6, or paint spec change affecting process)

| Phase                             | Module          | Impact                                                                                                                 |
| --------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1. Concept & Requirements         | **RQ Linker**   | Re-check compliance (corrosion resistance, strength, flammability, REACH/RoHS). Link updated RQs to affected features. |
| 2. 3D Modeling                    | **CAD CRUD**    | Update part metadata (`materialGrade`, density). New **functional** revision.                                          |
| 3. Material Calculation           | **MatCalc**     | **Direct impact**: mass, CO₂ per kg, and cost recomputed. BOM totals and LCA shift.                                    |
| 4. Simulation & Analysis          | **ProxyFEA**    | **Direct impact**: new material properties → different stress/thermal predictions (even if geometry is identical).     |
| 5. Manufacturing Planning         | **PathGen**     | **Potential impact**: feeds/speeds, tooling, weld parameters may change; cycle-time/manpower updates.                  |
| 6. Documentation & Change Control | **DocGen**      | **Major ECO** with material spec change; regenerate drawings, supplier packs, material callouts.                       |
| 7. Production & Assembly          | **MES Sync**    | **Direct impact**: push revised work orders; update routing if process parameters changed.                             |
| 8. Inspection & Testing           | **VisionQC**    | Update inspection criteria if surface finish/paint thickness or NDT requirements change.                               |
| 9. Deployment & In-Service        | **FieldLink**   | Tag the fielded assets with the new material revision for traceability (spares compatibility, corrosion watchlists).   |
| 10. Maintenance & Feedback        | **Prognostics** | **Direct impact**: RUL models adjust due to new material fatigue/corrosion behavior; service intervals may change.     |

# Practical tips

* **Decide “appearance vs. functional” early.** If it’s only color/texture, treat as a **minor ECO**; if material or process changes, treat as **major** and let MatCalc/PathGen/ProxyFEA/MES Sync propagate updates.
* **Keep `partUUID` stable** across both cases; bump **version IDs**. This preserves annotations and history.
* **VisionQC guardrail:** whitelist color changes in your CV pipeline so inspectors don’t get false positives.
* **DocGen templates:** separate **visual assets** (renders) from **spec tables** so appearance-only changes don’t trigger unnecessary supplier re-issues.

